  "notFrozen": [
    {
      "area": "Control reply envelope ({ok, code, error, result, capability, requestId})",
      "reason": "Not in the 0b list and its `result` is the open output of every registry command; the approval-granted reply carries a capability object whose fields were not re-derived. To freeze in 0c with the transport."
    },
    {
      "area": "Per-command argument grammar of the shell surface (SHELL_COMMANDS validators)",
      "reason": "Validators are code (branding JSON, plugin url schemes, panel names, voice actions); only the tier of each command is frozen here. The Rust host must reproduce them from control-authz.test.ts until they are moved into schemas."
    },
    {
      "area": "The registry command catalogue (ids, arguments, tiers of `ui`/`run` commands)",
      "reason": "Registered at run time by the renderer (src/store/os-commands.ts); it changes with the UI."
    },
    {
      "area": "Tool catalogue and per-tool argument schemas (C7)",
      "reason": "Dozens of built-in, MCP, plugin and skill tools, each with its own JSON-schema fragment; they change with every feature. Only the call / result / audit envelopes are covered, as provisional."
    },
    {
      "area": "User-facing wording (tool result text, refusal `reason` strings, French audit decisions)",
      "reason": "Localisable text. Tests assert on codes and tiers, never on prose, except where a test already pins a sentence."
    },
    {
      "area": "Open vocabularies: audit `code` values, bridge audit `decision` values",
      "reason": "New outcomes are added as features land; only their lexical shape is frozen."
    },
    {
      "area": "Capability / approval record layout (control-capability.ts)",
      "reason": "Internal to the host; only its journal fingerprint (12 hex) is frozen."
    },
    {
      "area": "Vault, approvals broker, supervisor, updater, D: volume",
      "reason": "Not yet extracted behind a seam; phases 1-4."
    }
  ]
}
